WEBVTT

00:29:28.375 --> 00:29:31.893
Then they turn around,
and they ascertain if you're still there.

00:29:31.917 --> 00:29:36.643
And if the base is safe,
they do turn around and they go further,

00:29:36.667 --> 00:29:41.101
and they are experiencing
security and risk at the same time.

00:29:41.125 --> 00:29:43.309
And that is the developmental
dance, I think.

00:29:43.333 --> 00:29:46.559
So I don't know which one,
maybe with some, you know --

00:29:46.583 --> 00:29:49.774
I have two boys, and actually,
it's an interesting example for this.

00:29:49.798 --> 00:29:51.059
I remember, I have one,

00:29:51.083 --> 00:29:53.434
first, he would go, then he would fall,

00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:56.143
then he would figure out
what to do in order not to fall.

00:29:56.167 --> 00:30:00.018
The other one would sit,
study everybody else falling,